  "headline_finding": "Both independent reviewers reconfirmed, via wholly disjoint from-scratch re-derivations, that RO3's subgroup positive control is genuine and maximally extreme, and that the Fisher-combined statistic's non-rejection at k~49-191 curves is a structural, floor-capped consequence (the shortfall to significance is more than double the maximum any single cell can contribute; billions of draws would be needed to close it), not a bug or an unrepresentative background sample. H-MONO-663fb4's status level is unchanged; its status_note is sharpened per both reviewers' converged recommendation: Fisher-combined sensitivity is demonstrated absent for the single/few-extreme-outlier case (redundant with the already-power-verified per-curve Holm test), entirely untested for the many-mild-curves case it was actually introduced for.",
